  "title": "21 Illegal Migrants Rescued",
  "description": "SAN DIEGO - The U.S. Coast Guard rescued 21 illegal migrants when their 25-foot panga was disabled and overloaded with 21 people onboard, 28 miles west of Del Mar, Calif., this morning. The Cutter Haddock, an 87-foot patrol boat, safely transferred all 21 people and towed the panga back to Sector San Diego. The migrants were transferred to U.S. Border Patrol agents. (U.S. Coast Guard Video/PA2 Jetta H. Disco)",
